  if(fl&&!fl.moon_jse)rows+=li(MOONS[fl.moon].name+' position',fl.note+'. Inferred †: the moon is placed at the spacecraft’s Jupiter-centred position at closest approach (JUPCRDS row within '+f(fl.jupcrds_dt_to_nearest_row_s||0,0)+' s) minus the spacecraft’s moon-centred offset ('+fl.file.split('/').pop()+'), using PHIO axes built from that same Jupiter-centred position (Z = Jovian pole, Y toward Jupiter, X = Y × Z). The same construction applied to the 34 passes that have a data-derived basis differs from it by at most 0.36° for passes closer than 3.3 radii. Result: '+f(Math.hypot(fl.moon_inf[0],fl.moon_inf[1],fl.moon_inf[2])/RJ,4)+' Rj from Jupiter','not in data','inferred position †, then moved at the circular-orbit rate for that distance; assumes a circular orbit in Jupiter’s equatorial plane about the pole axis');
